  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Irish Rule of Law International has been engaged in Malawi since 2011, working to enhance the rule of law, access to justice, and the protection of human rights. The programme objective is to enhance the rule of law and access to justice in Malawi (the project includes &quot;child diversion activities for children from prisons&quot;). In addition, the project supports the Gender Justice Unit (GJU) in carrying out GBV legal clinics targeting women and girls in Lilongwe and women with children that are in detention.</narrative>
  </description>
